From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LeadingLight <noreply@leadinglight.app>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 05:15:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Requests: what an agent asks, named once, answered once

Each question, approval or plan a structured agent asks is a request named
by its agent process's place in the log (its generation) and the agent's
own id: pending, recorded once an answer is written, resolved once the
agent takes it (the tool's result comes back, or Codex says so),
cancelled when withdrawn, expired when its process ends. The ledger is
rebuilt from the log. GET /v1/sessions/{name}/requests lists them;
POST .../requests/{id}/respond answers one with a command id, kept in the
conversation's requests.json before the answer is written, so a retry is
told the same receipt and a second answer is refused. request.changed
says which changed.
